1. Objective

Evaluate whether a simulated recovery authority can sign approval responses using a private key while an application verifies those responses using only a public key.

The test examines asymmetric key separation, response integrity, request binding, replay rejection, wrong-key rejection and fail-closed behaviour.

2. Implementation

The simulation implemented:

- Ed25519 private-key signing within the recovery authority.
- Public-key verification within the application.
- Canonical JSON serialization for signed response payloads.
- Response integrity verification.
- Request ID binding.
- In-memory replay detection.
- Rejection of malformed, modified and incorrectly signed responses.
- Simulated authority outage and restoration.

The application received the authority's public verification key. The application object did not receive the private signing key.

